# COVID-19 Lung CT Scan Classification using CNN

A deep learning-based medical imaging project that applies **Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs)** to classify lung CT scan images into **COVID-19** and **Non-COVID-19** categories.

This project focuses on **Recall (Sensitivity)** as the primary evaluation metric due to the high cost of false negatives in healthcare diagnosis.

---

## Project Overview

The COVID-19 pandemic highlighted the need for fast and accurate diagnostic methods. While PCR testing remains standard, CT scans provide valuable imaging evidence for detecting lung infections.

Manual interpretation of CT scans can be time-intensive and subject to variability. This project explores the use of deep learning to automate COVID-19 detection and support faster clinical decision-making.

The model performs **binary image classification** on lung CT scan images using a custom CNN architecture.

---

## Problem Statement

Early and accurate detection of COVID-19 is critical for treatment and containment. However, manual CT scan analysis by radiologists can be slow, especially under high patient volumes.

This project addresses this challenge by developing an AI-powered image classification model capable of detecting COVID-19 from lung CT scans.

---

## Objective

To build and evaluate a CNN model for automated classification of lung CT scan images into:

- COVID-19
- Non-COVID-19

